    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Chantilly was platted in 1913 by the Greater Charlotte Finance and Realty Company on a former dairy farm of about 250 acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ichantilly.com/chantilly-neighborhood-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "It began as one of Charlotte’s early streetcar suburbs, alongside Plaza Midwood, Wilmore and Wesley Heights.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.charlotteobserver.com/news/local/article307786730.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Most homes were built in the 1940s and 1950s, showcasing modest bungalows, Craftsman and ranch‑style architecture that still define the neighborhood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ichantilly.com/chantilly-neighborhood-history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1949 the Independence Boulevard expressway sliced through the original grid, leaving the northern section known as Commonwealth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ichantilly.com/chantilly-neighborhood-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After a period of decline in the 1970s and 1980s, the 2000s and 2010s saw Chantilly gentrify as central Charlotte neighborhoods grew more desirable.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ichantilly.com/chantilly-neighborhood-history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today Chantilly blends historic charm with modern updates, supported by a strong neighborhood association that hosts regular community events.",
